---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { HERBS_SPICES_DATA } from '../../lib/clinical_databases';

const spices = HERBS_SPICES_DATA.filter(item => item.category === 'spice');

const SITE_URL = (Astro.site || 'https://nutritioncolours.com').toString().replace(/\/$/, '');
const spicesSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "MedicalWebPage",
  "url": `${SITE_URL}/knowledge/spices`,
  "name": "Clinical Spices Database | Metabolic Nutrition",
  "description": "Explore the scientific, biochemical profiles of therapeutic spices used in metabolic reversal protocols."
};
---
<BaseLayout 
  title="Clinical Spices Database | Metabolic Nutrition" 
  description="Explore the scientific, biochemical profiles of therapeutic spices used in metabolic reversal protocols."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(spicesSchema)} />
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-20 space-y-16">
    <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-4">
      <span class="text-lime-600 dark:text-lime-400 font-black uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-[10px]">Botanical Pharmacopeia</span>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black text-emerald-950 dark:text-white brand-font leading-tight">
        Clinical Spices Database
      </h1>
      <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed text-sm md:text-base font-medium">
        Explore the biochemistry, primary mechanism, active compounds, and clinical dosage guidelines of therapeutic spices.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
      {spices.map((spice) => (
        <div class="bg-white dark:bg-stone-900 p-8 rounded-[40px] border border-stone-100 dark:border-stone-850 shadow-lg hover:shadow-2xl transition-all duration-350 hover:-translate-y-1 flex flex-col justify-between group">
          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 text-emerald-800 dark:text-lime-400 text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-wider px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full border border-emerald-100/40 dark:border-emerald-900/30">
                🌶️ Spice
              </span>
              <span class="text-[10px] text-stone-450 italic font-semibold">{spice.scientificName}</span>
            </div>

            <div class="space-y-2">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-emerald-950 dark:text-white brand-font group-hover:text-emerald-700 dark:group-hover:text-lime-400 transition-colors">
                <a href={`/herb/${spice.id}`}>{spice.name}</a>
              </h2>
              <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-455 text-[11px] leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 font-semibold">
                <span class="font-extrabold text-emerald-900 dark:text-lime-500">Mechanism:</span> {spice.primaryMechanism}
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
              {spice.activeCompounds.slice(0, 3).map((comp) => (
                <span class="bg-stone-50 dark:bg-white/5 text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 text-[9px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider px-2 py-1 rounded-md">
                  {comp}
                </span>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="pt-6 mt-6 border-t border-stone-50 dark:border-stone-850/60 flex items-center justify-between">
            <a 
              href={`/herb/${spice.id}`} 
              class="text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-emerald-900 dark:text-lime-400 hover:text-emerald-700 dark:hover:text-lime-300 transition-colors flex items-center gap-1.5 group/btn"
            >
              View Monograph
              <span class="transform group-hover/btn:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <section class="mt-20 pt-16 border-t border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-850">
      <div class="prose prose-emerald max-w-none text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300 bg-white dark:bg-stone-900 p-8 md:p-12 rounded-[40px] border border-stone-150/40 dark:border-stone-850/60 shadow-sm space-y-6">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-emerald-950 dark:text-white brand-font">Therapeutic Role & Clinical Integration of Spices</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          Therapeutic spices serve as concentrated sources of bioactive compounds that play key roles in modern clinical metabolic nutrition. From a biochemical perspective, the active molecules found in common culinary spices—such as curcumin in turmeric, gingerol in ginger, cinnamaldehyde in cinnamon, and piperine in black pepper—interact with vital cellular signaling pathways. These compounds are studied for their ability to downregulate pro-inflammatory cytokines, enhance insulin receptor sensitivity, and support hepatic detoxification enzymes. Unlike standard culinary use, clinical application requires precise, evidence-graded dosing protocols tailored to individual biomarker profiles.
        </p>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          In clinical protocols, spices are rarely utilized in isolation. Instead, they are combined strategically to exploit synergetic interactions that improve bioavailability. For example, pairing piperine with curcumin increases the systemic absorption of curcumin by up to 2,000%, illustrating the importance of pairing food components to optimize therapeutic outcomes. Registered dietitians and clinical practitioners emphasize that because these compounds exert powerful physiological effects, their integration must be carefully monitored. This is especially true for patients with pre-existing conditions like chronic kidney disease (CKD) or liver dysfunction, where mineral solute limits and detoxification capacities must be strictly managed to prevent organ overload.
        </p>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          Furthermore, our editorial board uses a strict evidence grading system to evaluate all spice monographs. Recommendations are categorized from Level A (validated by multiple randomized controlled trials) to Level D (based on historical consensus and expert panels). This system ensures that all protocols remain clinically safe and source-verified. Patients are encouraged to track their metabolic parameters, such as fasting blood glucose and inflammatory markers like hs-CRP, when integrating therapeutic doses of spices into their routines. Always consult a healthcare professional to ensure these lifestyle swaps are safely coordinated with standard medical treatments.
        </p>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          Through the <strong>Nutritional Color Code system (NutritionColours)</strong>, we highlight the visual indicators of these bioactives. The deep gold of turmeric or the rich red of cayenne pepper signifies the presence of specific polyphenols and capsaicinoids that correlate with targeted cellular defense mechanisms. Integrating these vibrant colors into the daily diet ensures a wide spectrum of phytonutrient support, helping patients achieve long-term health preservation, tissue recovery, and overall quality of life.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
